  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 3, L = 8, P = 26. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[4, 0, 4, 18, 1, 21, 5, 15], [15, 9, 25, 5, 24, 11, 12, 11], [10, 10, 22, 4, 1, 11, 22, 0]], sigma = [6, 2, 1, 4, 3, 7, 0, 5], B = [11, 4, 4, 1, 1, 11, 11, 11].",
